# BuildKit reads <Dockerfile>.dockerignore next to the Dockerfile instead of
# back/.dockerignore. The context is back/, but catalog only needs the
# generated Go code and its own directory: everything else (the legacy
# prototype in _legacy/, gen/python, gen/java, proto/, deploy/, .git, other
# services, local .env files) stays out of the build context.
*
!gen/go/
!services/catalog/

**/.env
**/.env.*
services/catalog/bin/
services/catalog/*.test
services/catalog/coverage.*
